Featuring a striking black and gold open-frame, lightened chassis, "Bones" stripped away heavy exterior armor plating to maximize speed, agility, and maneuverability. Tony designed its individual armor components—limbs, torso, and helmet—to decouple completely mid-flight, allowing each piece to fly independently using built-in micro-thrusters before snapping back together around Tony or targeting multiple enemies simultaneously.

In Iron Man 3, Mark XLI delivers one of the most iconic combat highlights during the House Party Protocol at the Norco oil rig: JARVIS commands "Bones" to detach into separate limbs, flying through multiple Extremis soldiers to knock them down before magnetically reassembling mid-air to continue the fight.
